{"authored" [{"question" "q-80138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\ ϕ & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={4}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =16+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =32 \\\\ R & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "08bcaf2275f6a7d81618e8747f39d4bcf31b9158c54efcd1c55ad80ea1df2f7c" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{60}^{∘})"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953859/state.json" "file_sha256" "560ef78c6fb5934771428cb87fb858683df27d69340a1c70ee81548a07fed595" "basis" 618 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/questio