56496facbcd125d957c87864399173e648ee5c33a802e6b683b31f993bc8" "basis" 887 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(2)^{2}+(5)^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+25 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =29 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "18fc56496facbcd125d957c87864399173e648ee5c33a802e6b683b31f993bc8" "basis" 887 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "acc111648e98b3a7ad24643b1110f946f793c19d0f12e1979e915333edd2152a" "basis" 887 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "18fc56496facbcd125d957c87864399173e648ee5c33a802e6b683b31f993bc8" "basis" 887 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{29}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "18fc56496facbcd125d957c87864399173e648ee5c33a802e6b683b31f993bc8" "basis" 887 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013884/state.json" "file_sha256" "861e92a9a2eb52d4dcc9779b8d2c9e9c5eb0aa88078bb7559fb5573c749faf4c" "basis" 1177 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013884/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{6} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ ϕ & =arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\ ϕ & =30\\,{\\,}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013884/state.json" "file_sha256" "861e92a9a2eb52d4dcc9779b8d2c9e9c5eb0aa88078bb7559fb5573c749faf4c" "basis" 1177 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013884/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013884/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7a30ee3bd372f4c1bcd64bf34773da5d03d311eaa04d1a7b4a25df653423902f" "basis" 1177 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013884/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-327714" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013884/state.json" "file_sha256" "861e92a9a2eb52d4dcc9779b8d2c9e9c5eb0aa88078bb7559fb5573c749faf4c" "basis" 1177 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013884/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-80138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-80138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\ ϕ & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={4}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =16+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =32 \\\\ R & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-80138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "294042bc73c5acbf2031821c431c49059725b62cca723248115aa3cbac2341c9"} {"question" "q-80138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-80138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{60}^{∘})"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})"] ["math" "4\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-80138" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-{45}^{∘})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-80139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-80139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=1 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =1+3 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =4 \\\\ R & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-80139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "294042bc73c5acbf2031821c431c49059725b62cca723248115aa3cbac2341c9"} {"question" "q-80139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-80139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-80139" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-107579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $0<ϕ<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-107579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for cosine gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\ ϕ & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-107579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "294042bc73c5acbf2031821c431c49059725b62cca723248115aa3cbac2341c9"} {"question" "q-107579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-107579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-107579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$\n\n$R=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(2)^{2}+(5)^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+25 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =29 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "294042bc73c5acbf2031821c431c49059725b62cca723248115aa3cbac2341c9"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{29}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-327714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-327714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{6} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ ϕ & =arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\ ϕ & =30\\,{\\,}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sha256" "695df4c2a3fcc5ab00f2960696239de6b79acfd6cc4bf9aba0cc707a0441b58e"} {"question" "q-327714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "294042bc73c5acbf2031821c431c49059725b62cca723248115aa3cbac2341c9"} {"question" "q-327714" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071565/state.json" "file_sh